", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 380930, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Tr9v8sFAkiTvFVNFpFQA2P", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 384549, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said in its description that it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nI haven't merged it. A code owner has to approve before it can go into main.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012hUwMfURtzYyShT4xkdwSc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01EsHBMMZaAUJpLcm5wM9dQh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013QfUceHVfE9tDUrPAZx1V9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0146VmXqM4LW2fX58ywzNtQX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MFp7G1JFTSKLj3mRVbxX3u", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014UMQCuiVnGJs8oCqzquHmr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012LzaZTfqYvysuUCxKDerag", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Tr9v8sFAkiTvFVNFpFQA2P", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py` documented banker's rounding (FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).\n\nThis switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` said in its description that it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed.\n- **PR:** #101 is at https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101.\n\nI haven't merged it. A code owner has to approve before it can go into main.", "type": "text"}]}]}